<title>UK: Abbey up after bid for Scottish Amicable.</title>
<headline>Abbey up after bid for Scottish Amicable.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Abbey National Plc were indicated higher on Friday after the UK retail banking group said that it had made a bid for life insurance company Scottish Amicable.</p>
<p>The shares jumped 10-1/2p to 779-1/2 by 0808 GMT in pre-market dealings.  </p>
<p>Abbey said it was proposing a bid of bid between 1.1 billion and 1.4 billion stg for Scottish Amicable, which has rejected</p>
<p>Market makers said if the offer is ultimately accepted, it would bode well for Abbey.</p>
<p>&quot;People are just looking at how well (Abbey) did with Scottish Mutual a few years ago,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>However, he added, there were few buyers of Abbey shares near the day's high of 782p.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
